     "text": "{\"cost\": 10, \"rationale\": \"Every exfiltration technique needs admin on the db, fileserver or backup host. Reaching that admin needs stolen_dbadmin, which needs admin_dc or admin_adfs. That in turn needs stolen_admin, which comes from kerberoasting via a foothold on the appserver or apiserver. The shortest chain is: (1) phish_workstation, which gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user in one step; (2) pivot_internal; (3) auth_appserver; (4) kerberoast_dc, giving stolen_admin; (5) auth_dc; (6) escalate_dc; (7) dump_dbadmin_dc; (8) auth_db; (9) escalate_db; (10) exfiltrate_db. Each step is required by the next, and no technique combines two links in this chain. The ADFS branch has the same length. Starting with exploit_web plus steal_user_cred costs 2 steps instead of 1 for phishing.\"}"
    }
